= Chemistry bibliography

= The Electrical Double Layer and the Theory of Electrocapillarity by David C. Grahame
{c}
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by David C. Grahame}
{title2=1947}
{title2=10.1021/cr60130a002}

Chemical Reviews 41(3), 441–501. Publisher: https://doi.org/10.1021/cr60130a002

Electrochemical Society primary-paper archive: https://knowledge.electrochem.org/estir/hist/hist-66-Grahame.pdf

Section VI, printed pp. 470–474, derives the diffuse-layer theory from Poisson and Boltzmann equations. Equations (43)–(48), printed p. 474, distinguish integrated charge, integral <capacitance> and differential <capacitance>. The archived PDF includes two preliminary pages before printed p. 441.

= Understanding the Extraordinary Flexibility of Polydimethylsiloxane through Single-Molecule Mechanics by Song Lu and others
{c}
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by Song Lu}
{title2=2022}

ACS Materials Letters 4, 329–335.

Publisher: https://doi.org/10.1021/acsmaterialslett.1c00655

The primary-paper abstract describes single-chain atomic-force measurements and calculations supporting the flexibility of <polydimethylsiloxane>. It is a modern material-property reference, not a source supplied with the historical exam.

= Properties of some rodlike polymers in solution by C.-P. Wong and others
{c}
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by C.-P. Wong}
{title2=1978}

Journal of <polymer> Science: <polymer> Symposia 65, 173–192.

Publisher: https://doi.org/10.1002/polc.5070650116

The primary-paper abstract reports light-scattering and viscometry characterization of relatively stiff synthetic <polymers> in solution.

= Thermodynamics of High Polymer Solutions by Paul J. Flory
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Paul J. Flory}
{title2=1942}
{title2=10.1063/1.1723621}

Journal of Chemical Physics 10, 51–61. https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1723621

Primary-paper scan: https://www.appliedpolymertechnology.org/uploads/1/0/8/8/108867241/jchemphys_10_51.pdf

The lattice model treats connected <polymer> segments and derives the nonideal combinatorial <entropy> before adding the energetic mixing contribution.

= Definition and classification of colloids by International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry
{c}
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}

https://list.iupac.org/reports/2001/colloid_2001/manual_of_s_and_t/node33.html

The official terminology section defines the <colloidal> range as roughly $1\,\mathrm{nm}$ to $1\,\mathrm{\mu m}$ in at least one dimension and classifies systems by dispersed and continuous constituents.

= Cylindrical Primary Lithium Handbook and Application Manual: Lithium Iron Disulfide by Energizer
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Energizer}

Manufacturer technical handbook, Form 12004-A, 17 pages in the inspected copy. Printed pp.3–4 describe metallic-lithium construction and two-stage iron-disulfide conversion discharge; printed p.16 identifies the product as nonrechargeable. A web upload directory is not treated as the original publication date.

https://energizer.com/eu/ukraine/wp-content/uploads/2024/05/lithiuml91l92_appman.pdf

= The Role of Lead in Suppressing Passivation of High Silver-Containing Copper Anodes During Electrorefining by Labone L. Godirilwe and others
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Labone L. Godirilwe}

International Journal of the Society of Materials Engineering for Resources 25(1), 137–144; the inspected issue header is April 2022, whereas the PDF also carries a 2021 copyright and 2020 acceptance. Cite the issue date rather than silently interpreting acceptance as publication. Sections 2–3 specify controlled Cu–Ag–Pb <anodes>, sulfate <electrolyte>, <electrorefining> and SEM/EDS/XRD characterization of slime.

https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/ijsmer/25/1/25_137/_pdf

