= Schulze-Hardy rule in the IUPAC Gold Book
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by IUPAC}

https://old.goldbook.iupac.org/html/S/S05501.html

Entry S05501, citing the 1972 <colloid> terminology manual, page 610. The definition establishes counterion-valence sensitivity; the sixth-power estimate additionally assumes the high-potential DLVO model.

= Stern-Volmer kinetic relationships in the IUPAC Gold Book
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by International Union of Pure and Applied Chemistry}
{c}

https://goldbook.iupac.org/terms/view/S06004

Official terminology entry S06004. Describes dependence of photophysical <quantum yields> on reagent concentration, including the linear dynamic-quenching relation underlying the <Stern-Volmer equation>.

= O2 A-band line parameters to support atmospheric remote sensing Part II by David A. Long and others
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by David A. Long}
{c}
{title2=2011}

Primary manuscript: https://tsapps.nist.gov/publication/get_pdf.cfm?pub_id=907932

Full title: O2 A-band line parameters to support atmospheric remote sensing. Part II: The rare isotopologues. Section 3, manuscript page 4, distinguishes rotational $N$ from total $J$ and states the odd-$N$ nuclear-spin statistical restriction for the dominant oxygen isotopologues.

