{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by Werner Uhl}
{c}
{title2=2000}

https://doi.org/10.1021/om000244s

Primary study in Organometallics, volume 19, pages 4536–4543. Its abstract identifies the open <carbaalane> with two $C=CHPh$ groups and reports their <hydroalumination> during conversion to a capped aluminium cube. This establishes that the unsaturated groups are real, but the abstract alone does not establish which <electron counting> convention the examination intended.

= Total synthesis of (±)-tirandamycin A by Philip DeShong and others
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{tag=Work by Philip DeShong}
{c}
{title2=1985}

https://doi.org/10.1021/ja00304a031

Primary synthetic study. Pages 5220–5221, Schemes II–III, report aqueous <hydrogen fluoride> conversion of related pyranones into a fused <lactone>. The accompanying discussion qualifies the relative <stereochemistry> as a mechanistic assignment rather than an unambiguous assignment from the reported <NMR spectroscopy>.

= Compilation of Thermal Properties of Hydrogen in Its Various Isotopic and Ortho-Para Modifications by Harold W. Woolley and others
{parent=Chemistry bibliography}
{c}
{tag=Work by Harold W. Woolley}

https://nvlpubs.nist.gov/nistpubs/jres/041/5/v41.n05.a03.pdf

Journal of Research of the National Bureau of Standards 41, 379–475 (1948), RP1932. DOI: https://doi.org/10.6028/jres.041.037

Section III.2 and table 12 give ortho–para equilibrium composition and compare state sums with spectral and thermal evidence. The compilation distinguishes fixed-composition <normal hydrogen> from equilibrium <spin isomers of hydrogen> mixtures. It supplies institutional thermodynamic data and theory, rather than answers to a particular examination.

